A car travels in a straight line up a slope, as shown in Fig. 3.1.

{{figure:figure_3_1.png}}

The car has mass 850 kg and travels with a constant speed of 9.0 m s$^{-1}$. The car’s engine exerts a force on the car of 2.0 kN up the slope.

A resistive force $F_D$, due to friction and air resistance, opposes the motion of the car.

The variation of $F_D$ with the speed $v$ of the car is shown in Fig. 3.2.

{{figure:figure_3_2.png}}
